<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0" xmlns:bc="http://bibliocommons.com/rss/1.0/modules/event/"><channel><title><![CDATA[Events | Toronto Public Library]]></title><description><![CDATA[Events RSS feed]]></description><link>https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/events</link><generator>BiblioCommons</generator><lastBuildDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 00:41:57 GMT</lastBuildDate><language><![CDATA[en-CA]]></language><!-- derived from events-page.xml on 2026-11-03: item 1 cancelled, item 2 virtual with no location, item 3 given a long tag-laden summary --><item><title><![CDATA[Introduction to Serger Sewing]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>Learn the basics of operating our serger, the Juki MO-735!&nbsp;&nbsp; In this class we will go over the basic operation and key functions of a serger sewing machine. Threading the machine and safety will be discussed.</p>
<p>Between three and five&nbsp;threads are routinely used&nbsp;to sew a seam, trim off the raw edges & finish the edges all at the same time with the&nbsp;Juki MO-735 serger.&nbsp; However, this workshop focuses solely on learning the 4-thread overlock stitch.</p>
<p></p>
<p> <strong><strong>This course is mandatory in order to book the serger</strong></strong>.&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><strong><strong>Children under 13 must be accompanied by an adult.</strong></strong><br></strong></p>
<p><strong>Registration requires a library card&nbsp;and begins October 20, 2026 at 12:30 p.m.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p>
<p><strong>Note: Your spot is guaranteed only for the first 5 minutes of the program.</strong><br></p>
<p><strong><br></strong></p>
